<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Coca-Cola buy of British bottler.</title>
<headline>EU clears Coca-Cola buy of British bottler.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday formally cleared a plan by Coca-Cola Enterprises Inc to take full control of British bottler Coca-Cola &amp; Schweppes Beverages Ltd (CCSB).</p>
<p>Coca-Cola Enterprises, the world's largest Coke bottler, is 45 percent owned by Coca Cola Co. It is acquiring control of CCSB from Cadbury Schweppes through its purchase of Amalgamated Beverages Great Britain Ltd.</p>
<p>CCSB bottles a variety of soft drinks in Britain, including Coca Cola, Schweppes mixers, Fanta, Sprite and Canada Dry.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that it had determined that CCSB was dominant in the British market and that the deal would transfer that dominance to Coca-Cola Enterprises and its part-parent, Coca Cola.</p>
<p>But it said that Coca Cola's role in CCSB was already so large that the deal would not strengthen its position.</p>
</text>
